        "title": "docs(browser): clarify JSON flag placement",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe browser CLI reference described `--json` as a common flag without showing that it is parsed at the `openclaw browser` level. One browser tool page also showed `openclaw browser status --json`, which can steer users toward putting the flag after the subcommand.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis updates the browser CLI reference to show the supported `openclaw browser --json status` ordering and fixes the matching browser tool example. The change is docs-only and does not alter CLI behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers following the browser docs get a command form that matches the current CLI parser and tests.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Verified the edited docs contain `openclaw browser --json status` and no longer use the misleading browser status example.\n- Runtime tests were not run because this is a docs-only change and the clean worktree has no `node_modules` installed.",
